      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test has several understandability issues:\n1. Four unused static provider methods (`arbitraryCodec`, `canonicalEncodings`, `canonicalGetSpecifier`, `specifier`) clutter the class but aren't referenced by any `@ParameterizedTest`\n2. Magic numbers `140` and `189` have no explanation (they bound the population codec specifier range 141–188 per the Pack200 spec)\n3. The byte-extraction loop is imperative and unlabeled\n4. Imports for unused items remain\n\nLet me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes the four unused parameterized-test provider methods, replaces the magic numbers `140`/`189` with named constants tied to the Pack200 spec range (141–188), renames variables for clarity (`bandHeaderBytes`, `bandHeaderStream`, `decoded`), and adds descriptive assertion messages — all while preserving the exact same method calls and assertions."
    }
